      "description": "Original MIT synthetic pixel ramps and graph, generated by build_example.py. sRGB ICC generated with LittleCMS; header date/optional ID fixed for reproducibility. EXIF orientation 6 is a display hint; source pixels remain stored unrotated. Explicit orientation uses fresh metadata before re-encoding to avoid stale geometry. PNG keeps RGBA16 pixels exactly and round-trips EXIF/XMP/ICC/CICP; JPEG uses explicit RGB8 conversion and is lossy. Native metadata readback must match before a buffer or file is emitted. JPEG CICP intentionally fails. No customer content.",
